<section class="lsec rv " id="compare" aria-labelledby="h-compare"><!-- DYNAMIC: $landing->sections[0] (compare) -->
 <div class="lw"><p class="eyb"><span>01 · Who to hire</span></p><h2 id="h-compare">Freelancer, Agency, or a Dedicated Developer: What Actually Matters</h2><p class="lead nar">Most businesses searching for a CRM developer in Pakistan are really deciding between three options: a freelance marketplace like Upwork or Fiverr, an offshore development agency, or a single dedicated developer working directly with you. Each one has a real tradeoff, and it’s worth being upfront about them instead of pretending one option fits every project.</p><div class="opts"><div class="op"><small>Option 1</small><h3>Freelance marketplace</h3><p>You’re vetting an individual you’ve never worked with, based on platform reviews and a profile. Quality varies enormously, and there’s a real risk of inconsistent availability once the contract starts.</p></div><div class="op"><small>Option 2</small><h3>Offshore agency</h3><p>Solves the reliability problem with a team and a process, but your requirements usually pass through a project manager to a developer you rarely speak with, and the person writing the code can change mid-project.</p></div><div class="op me"><small>Option 3</small><h3>Dedicated developer</h3><p>One point of contact for the entire project: the same person scoping the architecture, writing the code, and still available after launch. Costs more than the cheapest freelance listing and less than a full agency engagement.</p></div></div>
 <div class="tbl ctb" role="region" aria-label="Freelancer vs agency vs dedicated developer comparison" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Attribute</th><th scope="col">Freelance marketplace</th><th scope="col">Offshore agency</th><th scope="col" class=us>Working with me</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Who builds it</th><td data-l="Freelance marketplace">Varies, often subcontracted</td><td data-l="Offshore agency">Assigned team, can change mid-project</td><td data-l="Working with me" class=us><span class=ck>✓</span>Same person, start to finish</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Accountability</th><td data-l="Freelance marketplace">Platform dispute process</td><td data-l="Offshore agency">Account manager as a buffer</td><td data-l="Working with me" class=us><span class=ck>✓</span>Direct: you talk to the developer</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Communication</th><td data-l="Freelance marketplace">Inconsistent by individual</td><td data-l="Offshore agency">Often filtered through a PM</td><td data-l="Working with me" class=us><span class=ck>✓</span>Direct, same person every time</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cost structure</th><td data-l="Freelance marketplace">Lowest upfront, quality varies</td><td data-l="Offshore agency">Team overhead built into rate</td><td data-l="Working with me" class=us><span class=ck>✓</span>No agency markup, no race-to-bottom pricing</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Best fit</th><td data-l="Freelance marketplace">Small, one-off tasks</td><td data-l="Offshore agency">Large rollouts needing multiple specialists</td><td data-l="Working with me" class=us><span class=ck>✓</span>A CRM project needing one person who understands it end-to-end</td></tr></tbody></table></div><!-- DYNAMIC: $landing->comparison[] -->
 <aside class="hon"><b>Honest note</b><p>If your project genuinely needs five specialists working in parallel (a large enterprise rollout with multiple integrations happening simultaneously), an agency is the right call, and I’d tell you that upfront rather than take on more than one person can properly handle.</p></aside></div>
</section>

