 <div class="lw"><p class="eyb"><span>03 · Cost &amp; timeline</span></p><h2 id="h-cost">CRM Development Cost &amp; Timeline</h2><p class="lead nar">The honest answer is that CRM pricing depends heavily on modules, integrations and expected user load. Here’s the rough shape of what different project sizes typically look like.</p>
 <div class="cost"><div class="tbl cst" role="region" aria-label="CRM project timelines" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Project type</th><th scope="col" class="us">Typical timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Project type">Focused CRM MVP<small>Lead management, single team</small></th><td data-l="Typical timeline"><span class="tt">4–6 weeks</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Project type">Multi-tenant CRM<small>Multiple clients or branches</small></th><td data-l="Typical timeline"><span class="tt">8–14 weeks</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Project type">Enterprise CRM<small>With HRM / payroll integration</small></th><td data-l="Typical timeline"><span class="tt">3–5 months</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><!-- DYNAMIC: $landing->cost_rows[] -->
